-- title:
--   Bregman divergence $B_\Phi(z,a)$
-- statement:
--   The **Bregman divergence** generated by $\Phi$ is
--   $$B_\Phi(z,a)=\Phi(z)-\Phi(a)-\Phi'(a)(z-a).\tag{7}$$
--
--   For convex differentiable $\Phi$ it is nonnegative; for $\Phi(z)=(z-1)^2$ it is the squared error $(z-a)^2$. It is the loss in the Bayes risk $R_\Phi$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\Phi'$ is `deriv Φ`; it is evaluated only at points of the open interval $J$ on which $\Phi$ is smooth.
-- source:
--   Li–Zadik, Functional inequalities from the fundamental limits of Bayesian estimation, STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 5ea05e95…8ed487), Section 2.2, p.14 (PDF 14), display (7)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped ENNReal ContDiff

namespace PhiSobBayes

/-- The **Bregman divergence** generated by `Φ`: `B_Φ(z, a) = Φ(z) − Φ(a) − Φ′(a)(z − a)`.

Li–Zadik, *Functional inequalities from the fundamental limits of Bayesian estimation*, STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 5ea05e95…8ed487), Section 2.2, p.14 (PDF 14), display (7).

**Formalization Note** `Φ′` is `deriv Φ`; it is used only at points `a` of an open interval on which
`Φ` is smooth. -/
noncomputable def bregman (Φ : ℝ → ℝ) (z a : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  Φ z - Φ a - deriv Φ a * (z - a)

end PhiSobBayes


